(2.3 Step-by-Step Solved Board Problem) Tj
/F2 10 Tf
0 -20 Td
(Problem Statement: Calculate the total work done when a system expands reversibly from V1 to V2.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Solution Step 1: Write down the given initial parameters V1 = 2.0 L, V2 = 5.0 L, P = 1.013 x 10^5 Pa.) Tj
0 -15 Td
(Solution Step 2: Apply W = - P_ext * (V2 - V1) = - 1.013 x 10^5 * (3.0 x 10^-3) = -303.9 Joules.) Tj
(Final Result: Total Work Done by System = -303.9 J (Exothermic expansion)) Tj
